cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Lid-Driven Cavity Flow: a verified 2-D incompressible Navier-Stokes solver"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Toumi
    given-names: Marouane
version: 1.2.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A finite-difference solver for the two-dimensional incompressible
  Navier-Stokes equations in vorticity-streamfunction form, applied to the
  lid-driven cavity. Convection is treated explicitly with centered
  differences and diffusion implicitly, giving a semi-implicit scheme that is
  second order in space and first order in time. Wall vorticity is
  reconstructed with Thom's conditions. The implementation is verified by the
  method of manufactured solutions with observed orders of convergence
  measured in space and time separately. Cavity fields are compared with
  Ghia, Ghia and Shin (1982) at Reynolds numbers 400, 1000 and 3200, and with
  Botella and Peyret (1998) at Reynolds number 1000. Published reference
  anomalies and finite-time convergence limits are reported explicitly.
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - Navier-Stokes
  - lid-driven cavity
  - vorticity-streamfunction
  - finite differences
  - verification and validation
